{"markup": "<div data-component=\"page\" data-slug=\"privacy-policy\" data-name=\"page.legal\" data-v-f08e35e9><div data-component=\"legal\" _type=\"page.legal\" name=\"page.legal\" data-v-0d1be5c9><div data-component=\"transition-logo-mask\" data-v-0d1be5c9 data-v-24a16d5c><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\" data-v-24a16d5c><defs data-v-24a16d5c><clipPath id=\"v-0-0-0\" clipPathUnits=\"objectBoundingBox\" data-v-24a16d5c><path d=\"M0.5 0.459184C0.483235 0.501531 0.483824 0.506633 0.476471 0.540816H0.523529C0.516471 0.505612 0.514706 0.496429 0.5 0.459184Z\" data-v-24a16d5c></path></clipPath></defs></svg><div class=\"slot-wrapper\"  data-v-24a16d5c><div data-component=\"header\" _type=\"header\" data-v-0d1be5c9 data-v-31fc84b0><div class=\"header-wrapper\" data-v-31fc84b0><span data-component=\"tag\" data-force-active=\"false\" class=\"span-tag\" data-v-31fc84b0 data-v-a9cd5498><span class=\"label-container\" data-v-a9cd5498><span class=\"-sans-text-3-medium label\" data-v-a9cd5498>Privacy</span></span></span><h1 class=\"header-title xxl-18 xl-18 lg-20 md-22 sm-12 xs-14 -mix-title-3\" data-v-31fc84b0>Delta Cafés Privacy Policy</h1><h2 class=\"header-info\" data-v-31fc84b0><span class=\"-mix-text-2-regular\" data-v-31fc84b0>Updated</span><time class=\"-sans-text-3-medium\" datetime=\"2026-05-05\" data-v-31fc84b0>2026-05-05</time></h2></div></div><main data-v-0d1be5c9><div data-component=\"article-body\" _type=\"body\" data-v-0d1be5c9 data-v-f9679557><div class=\"article-body align-center\" data-v-f9679557><div class=\"article-content\" data-v-f9679557><p>This Privacy Policy governs the processing of personal data of users (hereinafter “User” or “Users”), collected in the context of their interactions with Manuel Rui Azinhais Nabeiro, Unipessoal, Lda. (“DELTA CAFÉS”), tax no. 500 853 975, with registered office at Avenida Calouste Gulbenkian, 7370-025, Campo Maior, as the entity responsible for the processing, namely through the use of the website [URL] (“Site”) for the disclosure and development of its commercial activities.</p><p>Visiting the Site by itself does not automatically register any personal data that identifies the User (except for data relating to the implementation of cookies that are strictly necessary for the operation of the site). However, completing contact forms will require the provision of personal data.</p><p>The provision of your personal data implies that you understand and accept the terms set out in this Privacy Policy. This Privacy Policy is complemented by the Website Terms and Conditions of Use and by the Cookies Policy.</p><p>This Privacy Policy includes information about:</p><p>A) Collection and processing of personal data;</p><p>B) Retention of personal data;</p><p>C) In which circumstances are data communicated to other entities;</p><p>D) Safety;</p><p>E) Data transfers to third countries;</p><p>F) Cookies;</p><p>G) Rights of data subjects;</p><p>H) Complaints;</p><p>I) Questions and suggestions;</p><p>J) Changes to the Privacy Policy.</p><p><strong>A) Collection and processing of personal data</strong></p><p>In your interactions with DELTA CAFÉS, you may provide us with personal data, which we will process for specific purposes.</p><p>**table** </p><p>Whenever your data is required to fulfil our legal obligations, to carry out pre-contractual steps, or to perform a contract, failure to provide it may prevent us from establishing a relationship with you.</p><p><strong>B. Retention of personal data</strong></p><p>The personal data collected are processed in strict compliance with the applicable legislation. The personal data will be stored in line with their specific purposes and in accordance with the applicable legal time limits. Therefore, and whenever there is no specific legal requirement, the data will be stored and kept only for an appropriate period and to the extent necessary for the purposes for which they were collected, unless, within the limits of the law, the right to object or the right to erasure is exercised, or consent is withdrawn.</p><p><strong>C. In which circumstances are data transmitted to other entities</strong><br><br>Your data may be transmitted by DELTA CAFÉS in the following situations:</p><p>1. When we use other entities to provide certain services, this provision of services may involve those entities accessing your personal data. Any subcontracted entity of DELTA CAFÉS will therefore process your personal data on our behalf and in accordance with our instructions, under the subcontracting agreement concluded with those entities.</p><p>2. To third-party entities, when it considers such data disclosures necessary or appropriate (i) in light of the applicable law, (ii) for compliance with legal obligations/court orders, (iii) with decisions or determinations of supervisory authorities, or (iv) to respond to requests from public or governmental authorities.</p><p>In all cases, DELTA CAFÉS undertakes to take all appropriate measures to ensure the effective protection of personal data.</p><p><strong>D. Safety</strong></p><p>DELTA CAFÉS makes its best efforts to protect Data Subjects’ personal data against unauthorised access. For this purpose, it uses security systems, rules, and other procedures to ensure the protection of personal data and to prevent unauthorised access, improper use, disclosure, loss, or destruction.</p><p><strong>E. Data transfers to third countries</strong></p><p>DELTA CAFÉS seeks to ensure that the processing of your personal data takes place within the European Economic Area. However, if this is not possible and your personal data are transferred to third countries (located outside the European Union or the European Economic Area) or to international organisations, for the purposes set out in this Policy, such transfers will be carried out (i) where there is an adequacy decision by the European Commission for the recipient country, (ii) to entities based or located in the United States of America (USA) that are certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework mechanism, or (iii) in all other cases, on the basis of appropriate safeguards, such as standard contractual clauses for data protection adopted by the European Commission.</p><p>In this case, DELTA CAFÉS undertakes to adopt appropriate security measures to ensure the confidentiality and protection of personal data, under the applicable legislation on personal data protection. In particular, the transferred data will be subject to the appropriate safeguards provided for by law, and additional measures will be ensured so that the personal data enjoy a level of protection that is essentially equivalent to that in force in the European Union.</p><p>You may request additional information by sending a written request to privacy@gruponabeiro.com.</p><h2></h2><p><strong>F. Cookies</strong></p><p>The Site uses cookies. To learn more, please refer to our Cookies Policy.</p><p><strong>G. Rights of data subjects</strong></p><p>Under the applicable legislation, the Data Subject may, at any time, request access to the personal data concerning them, as well as its rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, portability of their data, or object to its processing.</p><p>The Data Subject may also obtain confirmation as to whether personal data concerning them are being processed and, if requested, will be provided with a copy of the data undergoing processing.</p><p>Under the law, the Data Subject is also guaranteed the right to withdraw their consent to the processing of data for the stated purposes. This does not, however, invalidate the processing carried out up to that date on the basis of the consent previously given.</p><p>To exercise these rights or any of the above-mentioned rights, the Data Subject may submit a written request to the email privacy@gruponabeiro.com.</p><p><strong>H. Complaints</strong></p><p>Without prejudice to any other form of administrative or judicial remedy, the User has the right to lodge a complaint with the competent supervisory authority under the law, if they consider that the processing of their data by DELTA CAFÉS breaches the legal framework in force at any given time.</p><p><strong>I. Questions and suggestions</strong></p><p>Data Subjects may contact DELTA CAFÉS about any matter related to the processing of their personal data and to the exercise of the rights granted to them by the applicable legislation, as referred to in this Policy, via the email privacy@gruponabeiro.com.</p><p><strong>J. Changes to the Privacy Policy</strong></p><p>DELTA CAFÉS reserves the right to change these personal data processing terms at any time. These changes will be published on the Site and/or communicated to Users through the contact details provided.</p></div></div></div></main><footer data-component=\"footer\" data-v-0d1be5c9 data-v-955ea654><div data-component=\"pre-footer\" _type=\"preFooter\" class=\"pre-footer\" data-v-955ea654 data-v-669d83ae><div class=\"background-container\" data-v-669d83ae><img width=\"3400\" height=\"1966\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\" data-nuxt-img onerror=\"this.setAttribute(&#39;data-error&#39;, 1)\" data-component=\"media-asset\" alt=\"Image\" fetchpriority autoplay playsinline=\"true\" muted class=\"media\" data-v-669d83ae data-v-ac455cf8 src=\"/assets/images/7d844bfe2ad433e6df520232098d9147349f3d5a-3400x1966-26a59294f1.jpg\"></div><div class=\"content-container\" data-v-669d83ae><div class=\"upper-title-container\" data-v-669d83ae><div class=\"-mix-label-1 -uppercase upper-title\" data-v-669d83ae>Coffee Science Centre</div><div class=\"-mix-label-1 -uppercase upper-title-overlay\" data-v-669d83ae>Coffee Science Centre</div></div><div class=\"title-container\" data-v-669d83ae><div data-component=\"font-pairing-title\" class=\"title-2 -uppercase title\" data-v-669d83ae data-v-b55614a0><h2 class=\"title\" data-v-b55614a0><span>Science <em>and</em>Know-How</span><span>united<em>by</em>Art</span></h2